DATA SECURITY AND PRIVACY

BlackBar MCP may process personal information,
health information and other sensitive data.

Operators are responsible for ensuring that
processing is authorized and compliant with
applicable privacy, confidentiality and
data protection requirements.

Appropriate security controls should be
implemented for:

- Unity Catalog Volume access
- Application authentication
- Model endpoint permissions
- Temporary file handling
- Processing logs
- Generated output files
- Retention and deletion policies

AUTOMATED REDACTION LIMITATIONS

BlackBar MCP uses a combination of language
models, speech recognition, document parsing
and deterministic media-processing algorithms.

These technologies may produce errors,
including failures to detect sensitive content.

The application does not guarantee complete
anonymization or removal of all personal data.

Automated redaction results should be verified
before external disclosure, production use
or processing in regulated environments.

The successful creation of an output file
does not itself establish that all sensitive
information has been removed.

